A||||16||Phantom Rage||120mph gauge swap||||5||
Z||000000||Phantom Rage||07-09-2000||04:29 PM||||Ok, I got the 120mph gauge installed.  All seems to work fine, including the odometer swap.  <P>I ran across two problems though:<P>1) Looks like I will need a different black faceplate to cover the edges of the gauges.  The one on my 85mph gauge has an outer ring to cover any light bleed, the 120 does not.  Not a problem here, can get at bone yard. This is just info for anyone thinking about doing the swap.<P>2) Gauge illuminates brighter than my other gauges.<BR>Not sure what to do here, any suggestions?  <P>As always, Thankyou  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Phantom Rage (edited 07-09-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||07-09-2000||04:31 PM||||Are you trying to swap a 120MPH into a steel face (vs plastic face) 85 MPH?<P>I suggest you get an plastic face cluster assembly. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ggarsk||07-09-2000||07:23 PM||||Phantom,what year care did you put your speedo in? I put one in my '84 and the speeedo is off 3mph at 25. I don't know exactly how much the odometer is of but it is enough to lose 5+ mpg on fuel consumption. Not actual decrease but in the difference on the readings. The circuit boards and odometer motors are different from the '84 and the newer models. Dores anybody know if I need a new gear  to correct this?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||07-09-2000||08:58 PM||||Phantom Rage--Find a set of gauges out of an '86SE.  They have the 85mph speedo, but they're backlit so you'll eliminate one of the problems.  Your 120mph speedo will fit perfectly.  You can find the '86SE gauges for around $30.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phantom Rage||07-10-2000||05:39 AM||||Thanks guys, I was looking at my brother’s Formula and the plate does look different, hopefully I can find one in the bone yard sometime this week.<P>Terryk/Monkeyman, I was thinking I might be able to use one from any 2.8L since they came with the 6g tach.  If I remember right, most of the 6g tach's I have seen don't have the outer rim; I'm not really sure though.  There was an 86SE at the bone yard last week; hopefully the plate is still intact.<P>GGarsk, I think I got the gauge form an 86GT, if there is even such a beast.  I put it into an 88 4cyl coupe. The funny thing is my brother said the same thing about speed variances. When time permits, we will try to match one another at various speeds. <P>Thanks Again <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000005||Monkeyman||07-10-2000||11:47 AM||||I think the only years/models to get the 120mph speedo were the '86-'88 GTs and the '88 Formula.  All the rest had an 85mph speedo (even the '85 GT).  My gauges are from an '87 GT (in my '85 GT now).  My tach is messed up, but I'll probably just swap it with the tach from my '86SE gauges whenever I get up the nerve.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fret Naught||07-10-2000||03:11 PM||||Hum, that is interesting, I have an 86SE, and the speedo, decal? you know the thing with the numbers on it is all kind of bubbly, I can see it in the day time, but at night it doesn't show up very well. I have been looking for a replacement. Mine goes up to 150 MPH ? I assumed it was stock? any body else have one that goes up to 150 MPH?||||reg||5
Z||000007||Monkeyman||07-10-2000||10:41 PM||||150mph?  Not from the factory.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fret Naught||07-11-2000||01:04 AM||||Its not hum, well it seems to be accruate, any suggestions on replacing it with a 120? seems like if I were to just replace it that it would need to be re-calibrated? Though the distance between say 50 and 60 is so small, that you just sort of guess at 55, there is no graduated marks? So maybe a 120 would go right on. What do you guys think?||||reg||4
Z||000009||TheFiero64||07-11-2000||01:47 PM||||Hey Fret, Your side of the country still has <B>55</B> for a speed limit? In MA we changed to <B>65</B> about 5 years ago. I think some states even go up to 75.<P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000010||Fret Naught||07-11-2000||02:48 PM||||Nope, we are up there with the rest of you except on rural roads or hwys. in and around populated areas then it drops to 55.||||reg||1
Z||000011||batboy||07-11-2000||07:45 PM||||Fret, I've heard of kits for 150 or 160 and even 200 MPH speedo kits. I think they put a new face decal on and change some of the electronics to allow it to read correctly. If you get a stock 120 MPH GT speedo, it will fit right in and work just fine.||||reg||1
Z||000012||rogergarrison||07-11-2000||09:05 PM||||my 86 has a 'thru the face' lighting. I used thinner to clean off all the numbers and put on a new decal face from The Fiero Store that reads 200 mph. You remove the needle by pulling it off the shaft with your fingers. i then used a portable GPS and drove it up to exactly speed of 70 mph, and pushed the needle back on so it showed 70. Its only a few miles off either above or below that. I can live with 37 at an actual 35, and over a 100 who really cares if its really 2 or 3 miles off. New face was only $35 and blows peoples minds when they see the dash.<P>rg<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fret Naught||07-12-2000||01:10 AM||||Thanks for the input I don't know where I would get my hands on a GPS, and if I did I am not sure I would know what to do with it. Bat boy I have a dumb ? If I get a spedo out of a GT, for a swap, won't I end up changing everything tach odometer etc... I thought it was all one unit Eda kate me Ole Wise one!!! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000014||Monkeyman||07-12-2000||12:27 PM||||The speedo and the tach just pull out of the cluster.  There are some metal clips on the cluster and some ?? (looks like the threaded end of a bolt) on the back of the gauges.  Once you remove the face (both plastic and other), you can just pull (gently, please) the gauges out.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000015||Fret Naught||07-12-2000||12:30 PM||||Cool, now all I need to do is find a replacement,<BR>thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000016||batboy||07-12-2000||09:28 PM||||Yeah, what Monkey said. It is easier and quicker if you get the whole cluster, but all the gauges pull out separately. Well, the temp and the fuel gauge are together as one unit. Also the tach that goes with the 85 MPH speedo will have the oil pressure gauge built into it. The 120 MPH tach doesn't, because that option also put a ralley pod on top climate control and radio hump that contained an oil and a volt gauge. You can just put the speedo in by itself if you want though.||||reg||1
